mastery.question_text:
$T$ is the point of contact of a tangent to a circle, centre $O$.
$TA$ is a chord, and $\angle OTA = \beta$.
$B$ is a point on the circle in the alternate segment.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (T) at (0,2.2);
\coordinate (L) at (-1.2,2.2);
\coordinate (R) at (1.2,2.2);
\draw (O) circle (2.2);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below] at (O) {$O$};
\draw (L) -- (R);
\node[above] at (T) {$T$};
\coordinate (A) at (1.905,-1.1);
\draw (T) -- (A);
\coordinate (B) at (-2.067,-0.752);
\draw (T) -- (B);
\draw (A) -- (B);
\draw (T) -- (O) -- (A);
\node[left] at (B) {$B$};
\node[right] at (A) {$A$};
\pic[draw, "$\beta$", angle radius=0.5cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=O--T--A};
\pic[draw, "$\alpha$", angle radius=0.6cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=A--T--R};
\pic[draw, "$x$", angle radius=0.5cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=A--B--T};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Prove that the tangent-chord angle $\alpha$ equals $\angle TBA = x$.

